+                whatever resolution the stream actually negotiates, so 800000 means 800 kbps
+                at 720p and about 1.8 Mbps at 1080p. Frame rate is not part of the scaling.
+                Holding the bitrate fixed while the resolution changed is how a 1080p stream
+                ended up on a 720p budget, where the camera keeps bits-per-pixel constant and
+                drops frame rate instead - 30 fps became 13.
 
